 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T16:45+08:00",
 "answer": "**I’d skip cycling this evening.** Kuching’s latest reading I found was **API 69 (moderate) at 3 pm today, October 17**—not the worst category, but haze plus hard exercise means breathing in more particles. ([jerebumalaysia.com](https://jerebumalaysia.com/negeri/sarawak/?utm_source=openai))\n\nMore importantly, **thunderstorms are forecast around 6–8 pm**, so riding conditions may be unsafe regardless of the haze. \n\nIf you do go out, keep it short and easy, check the latest official **APIMS** reading first, and turn back if you notice coughing, wheezing, or throat or eye irritation. If you have asthma or a heart/lung condition, avoid the ride. ([malaymail.com](https://www.malaymail.com/news/malaysia/2026/10/09/haze-doe-urges-public-to-refer-to-official-api-readings-amid-differences-across-platforms/238373?utm_source=openai))",
